  "excerpt": "Peperoni ripieni are whole peppers stuffed with a herb-and-rice filling, baked until the pepper is very soft and the filling is cooked through. The Italian version uses a combination of rice, herbs, Parmigiano, and olive oil rather than meat or breadcrumbs, giving a lighter, fragrant result suited to late summer when peppers are at their best.",
