  "sourceNotes": "Peperoni ripieni is common throughout Italian cooking, with regional variations across Lazio, Campania, Piedmont, and Sicily. The rice-based filling is common in the Italian south; northern versions sometimes use meat. The dish is part of the Italian stuffed vegetable tradition.",
